  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "disco house (French touch, filter disco): the four, a clap on two and four, the open hat on every and that disco is named by, sixteenth closed hats, a bouncing root-and-fifth bass and chopped chord stabs on the offbeats",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar of drums and two of chords. Disco's octave bass is out of reach — the bass register refuses a recipe line wider than seven semitones on some keys — so the bounce is root and fifth. The stabs are a bright struck keyboard on the and of two and the and of four, the filtered-sample loop of the style played as notes; the filter sweep across them is the stage's, which a row cannot ask for."
  }
